From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: link the X11 and RandR libraries

system.cpp calls XOpenDisplay and the XRandR API, but the CMake target does
not link either library. Match the libraries already used by upstream's
Makefile and Nix packaging so the CMake build resolves those symbols.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@ file(GLOB SRC_FILES src/*.cpp)
 
 add_executable(lapifetch ${SRC_FILES})
 
+target_link_libraries(lapifetch PRIVATE X11 Xrandr)
+
 include(GNUInstallDirs)
 
 install(TARGETS lapifetch
